================================================================================
Easy Modules Unified — Riftbound fork (not MIT)
================================================================================

scripts/objects/b93b40_tyrantnomad_s_easy_modules_unified.lua is a Riftbound
adaptation of TyrantNomad's Easy Modules Unified. MTG-only UI is stripped; Might
and Riftseer re-import modules target this save's Encoder and importers. Not
listed under MIT; credit TyrantNomad and Tipsy Hobbit (Encoder) as above.

================================================================================
Domain counters and other reskins (not MIT)
================================================================================

Domain counter bags (Calm, Body, Fury, Chaos, Mind, Order) use scripts
derived from the fork's MTG mana-colour counter bags. They are reskinned and
relabeled for Riftbound (port complete on-table) but are not listed under MIT.
Credit the upstream table authors above.

Score Tracker objects (Amuzet / π lineage, might-token layout by this fork)
and other upstream counter bags (+1, generic, text, drop-on-card) follow the
same rule: reskins may use MIT art URLs in the save without MIT-licensing the
underlying Lua.

================================================================================
πKeywords card tokens (not MIT)
================================================================================

scripts/objects/ae12d3_keywords.lua (Encoder object GUID ae12d3) drives the
πKeywords property on encoded cards. It is adapted from Tipsy Hobbit's Keyword
Abilities module and integrated via TyrantNomad's Easy Modules / πKeywords
suite. This fork replaces MTG keyword names and mechanics with a Riftbound
counter and status set (`rb_*` keys; legacy `mtg_*` removed). Not listed under
MIT; credit Tipsy Hobbit and TyrantNomad as above. Physical keyword token bags
were removed from the table; on-card πKeywords remain the supported path.

================================================================================
Tiles and docs still showing upstream MTG text (not MIT)
================================================================================

Table Instructions (`e40450`) and Chat Commands (`7b59f7`) tiles still display
legacy MTG copy. πMenu colour-filter variables in global.lua still use WUBRGC
names. These are tracked for cleanup in Components.md ("MTG remnants in code");
they remain upstream-derived content in the save until rewritten.

